"""Readable standalone explanation accompanying the row audit."""
import html,json,sys
from pathlib import Path
sys.path.insert(0,str(Path(__file__).parent))
from report import CAUSES,RULES
out=Path(sys.argv[1]);root=Path(__file__).parent
m=json.loads((out/'report-summary.json').read_text());examples=json.loads((out/'examples.json').read_text())
def e(v):return html.escape(str(v if v not in (None,'') else '—'))
def n(v):return f'{v:,}'
def table(headers,rows):return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(v)+'</th>' for v in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+e(v)+'</td>' for v in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
def fields(d,keys):return '<dl>'+''.join('<dt>'+e(label)+'</dt><dd>'+e(d.get(k))+'</dd>' for k,label in keys)+'</dl>'
rows=[]
for c,(label,total) in CAUSES.items():
 z=m['categories'][c];a=z.get('already_live_recovered',0);b=z.get('new_conservative_support',0);q=z.get('extra_conditional_support',0)
 rows.append([label,n(total),n(a),n(b),n(q),n(total-a-b-q)])
t=m['totals'];a=t.get('already_live_recovered',0);b=t.get('new_conservative_support',0);q=t.get('extra_conditional_support',0)
rows.append(['TOTAL','36,102',n(a),n(b),n(q),n(36102-a-b-q)])
body='<h1>Can these five problem groups be reduced?</h1><p class="lead">A fixed-cohort DXBI matching experiment. Every proposed link keeps the sale amount within AED 2. Original spreadsheet fields are preserved.</p>'
body+='<div class="tiles"><div><strong>'+n(q)+'</strong>additional conditional candidates</div><div><strong>'+n(m.get('conditional_date_status',{}).get('exact_date',0))+'</strong>also match the exact date</div><div><strong>'+n(36102-a-b-q)+'</strong>still not supported by either profile</div></div>'
body+='<p><b>Supported means that the row passed the stated rules.</b> It does not mean independently verified ownership. Conditional rows use a broader assumption and are separated from conservative results. Tentative and extreme suggestions do not reduce the remaining count.</p>'
body+='<h2>The numbers, without double counting</h2>'+table(['Starting issue','Original rows','Already matched','New conservative','Extra conditional','Remaining'],rows)
body+='<p>Each original row appears once. The total is 36,102 rows, representing '+n(m['unique_source_events'])+' source events. Buyer and seller rows may describe the same sale. These are not 36,102 different owners or properties. The other 74,225 named rows and 539 nameless rows were outside this experiment. A row can have several defects, but its original bucket stays fixed: most damaged Damac location labels were in the missing-identifier bucket, so recovering those rows reduces that bucket.</p>'
body+='<p>The “already matched” column separates eight rows that the live backend had resolved before this experiment. New conservative and extra conditional columns are disjoint. No proposed links were written to the live backend.</p>'
body+='<h2>The rules in plain language</h2>'
for code,title,detail in RULES:body+='<details '+('open' if code in ('R1','R5','R6','R8a / C1','R8b / C2','R8c / C3','R8d / C4','R8e / C5','R9') else '')+'><summary>'+e(code+' · '+title)+'</summary><p>'+e(detail)+'</p></details>'
body+='<h2>The source-data defect we found</h2><p>The Damac sheet contains an exact sequence from row 11,086 to row 28,378: DAMAC HILLS 3, DAMAC HILLS 4, …, DAMAC HILLS 17295. Every suffix equals the row number minus 11,083. This strongly suggests an accidental spreadsheet fill sequence. It affects 13,815 rows inside these five groups, including 13,244 of the 13,563 missing-identifier rows. Independent matched properties from the same sheet support Damac Hills 2 as the intended community. The repair is conditional and preserves the original label; it does not by itself prove which unit or sale belongs to a row.</p>'
body+='<h2>Why we cannot fix everything by being more forgiving</h2><p>For the original 6,053 “property found, no sale within AED 2” rows, a separate history check found no sale on the previously linked property for 3,292 rows. The other 2,761 have a closest recorded sale outside the price tolerance: four differ by more than AED 50 and at most AED 1,000; 107 by more than AED 1,000 and at most AED 10,000; and 2,650 by more than AED 10,000. A previous property link may itself be wrong. These are diagnostic references, not additional matches.</p>'
body+='<p>For example, Greens JAN 2025.xlsx / Old / row 280 names Al Ghozlan 4, unit G10, AED 720,000 on 5 September 2021. The closest captured sale on that previously linked property is AED 1,215,000 on 1 May 2025—a difference of AED 495,000. That may be a later sale of the same unit; it cannot satisfy the source transaction’s AED 2 rule. Likewise, a missing unit is different from a contradictory unit. If the sheet says unit 402 and DXBI says 403, an identical price does not establish that one of them is a typo. And two nearby units can sell for the same round amount on the same date.</p>'
ext=json.loads((root/'actual-rule-extents.json').read_text())
body+='<h2>Exactly how far the relaxed rule goes</h2><p>The allowed amount difference is AED 2; among these 2,776 proposals the largest actual difference is AED '+e(ext['price_gap_max_aed'])+'. Size remains within the greater of 50 sqft or 2%. The date-relaxed profile has <b>no maximum date gap</b>, because it instead requires one surviving event across the entire captured community/price/size history.</p><p>That produces a maximum date difference of <b>'+n(ext['date_gap_max_days'])+' days (about 7.6 years)</b>. Of the 834 date-relaxed rows, '+n(ext['date_gap_over_365_rows'])+' differ by more than one year, '+n(ext['date_gap_over_730_rows'])+' by more than two years, and '+n(ext['date_gap_over_1825_rows'])+' by more than five years. These thresholds overlap; do not add them. Such gaps may reflect different registration stages, but they are not proof that the source owner belongs to that recorded sale.</p>'
worst=ext['extreme_date_examples'][0];wr=worst['source_raw'];wt=worst['target']
body+='<article class="risk"><h3>Most aggressive proposed link</h3><p>'+e(worst['source_file'])+' · '+e(worst['source_sheet'])+' · row '+e(worst['source_row'])+'</p>'+table(['Field','Original source','Proposed DXBI'],[['Location',wr.get('master_project'),str(wt.get('area_name'))+' / '+str(wt.get('building_name'))],['Unit',wr.get('unit_number'),wt.get('unit_number')],['Amount AED',wr.get('transaction_price_aed'),wt.get('sale_amount_aed')],['Date',wr.get('transaction_date'),wt.get('transaction_date')],['Size',str(wr.get('size_unknown'))+' (learned sqm)',str(wt.get('size_sqft'))+' sqft']])+'<p><b>Review only:</b> this combines a repaired location, an inferred unit and a 2,765-day date difference. It is included in the 834 riskier proposals, not the 1,942 exact-date candidates.</p></article>'
body+='<h2>Original row → proposed DXBI link</h2><p>These examples progress from supported links to conditional and risky suggestions. Red examples show what forcing a match would introduce; they are not accepted recoveries. The workbook contains the full filtered ledger and more examples.</p>'
used=set();cards=[]
for x in examples:
 key=(x['status'],x['original_cause'],(x.get('conditional_profile') or {}).get('profile'))
 if key in used:continue
 used.add(key);cards.append(x)
for x in cards:
 status=x['status'];cls='good' if status=='new_conservative_support' else 'conditional' if status=='extra_conditional_support' else 'risk'
 raw=x['source_raw'];target=x['target']
 body+='<article class="'+cls+'"><h3>'+e(status.replace('_',' '))+'</h3><p>'+e(x['original_cause'])+'<br><b>'+e(x['source_file'])+'</b> · '+e(x['source_sheet'])+' · row '+e(x['source_row'])+'</p><div class="compare"><section><h4>What the sheet actually had</h4>'+fields(raw,[('area_name','Area'),('master_project','Master project'),('project_name','Project'),('building_name','Building'),('unit_number','Unit'),('building_number','Building number'),('plot_number','Plot number'),('property_number','Property number'),('property_type','Type'),('transaction_price_aed','Amount AED'),('transaction_date','Date'),('size_unknown','Size without unit'),('size_sqft','Declared sqft'),('size_sqm','Declared sqm')])+'</section><section><h4>DXBI candidate</h4>'+fields(target,[('area_name','Area'),('project_name','Project'),('building_name','Building'),('unit_number','Unit / villa / plot'),('property_type','Type'),('sale_amount_aed','Sale amount AED'),('amount_aed','Amount AED'),('transaction_date','Date'),('size_sqft','Size sqft')])+'</section></div><p><b>Rule:</b> '+e(x['rule'])+'<br><b>Decision:</b> '+e(x['reason'])+'<br><b>Price gap AED:</b> '+e(x['amount_gap_aed'])+'</p>'
 cp=x.get('conditional_profile') or {}
 if cp.get('community_repair'):body+='<details><summary>Location repair and independent support</summary><pre>'+e(json.dumps(cp['community_repair'],indent=2))+'</pre></details>'
 proof=(cp.get('selected') or {}).get('production_namespace_proof')
 if proof:body+='<p><b>Why the different-looking codes agree:</b> the full original code supplies the community, cluster and child number; the original named project and numeric label agree with that same namespace.</p><details><summary>Full namespace proof</summary><pre>'+e(json.dumps(proof,indent=2))+'</pre></details>'
 if x['conflicts']:body+='<p><b>Original checks retained (see namespace proof where present):</b> '+e(', '.join(x['conflicts']))+'</p>'
 body+='</article>'
body+='<h2>Your AFMU019B example</h2><p>In Furjan JAN 2025.xlsx, sheet “apr to dec”, row 2146, the source PropertyNo is AFMU019B and the type is Commercial Plots. The captured DXBI data also contains the full plot code AFMU019B. Keeping the entire code makes sense; chopping it to “villa 19B” does not. That source row has no explicit sale event and is outside these five issue groups, so it is not counted as a recovery here.</p>'
body+='<h2>How the experiment was checked</h2><p>Learning uses earlier accepted links as weak labels, split by connected source unit and DXBI property so the same property does not train and test itself. Alias and learned size-unit inference use only the training partition. C2–C5 are exploratory extensions assessed on the same weak-label holdout after earlier aggregate results; their agreement is not an independent accuracy estimate. The structured-code namespace rule is a separate post-hoc proposal: its candidates were checked against full price pools and positive controls, but it has no blind holdout accuracy estimate. The damaged-label subset has zero repaired examples in that masked holdout: its support comes from the exact source-row pattern, independent sheet context and candidate checks, not a measured repair accuracy rate. C2–C4 may instead infer a size unit from the candidate, which is a separate stated assumption. Missing-identifier tests hide the child identifiers; retained encoded identifiers are audited separately. The validation results in the accompanying files measure agreement with earlier links, not real-world owner accuracy.</p><p>All original rows are reconciled, all candidate pools are uncapped, the SQLite snapshot is opened read-only, and the live backend tables are compared before and after. See the audit files for exact checks and any limitations.</p>'
vr=json.loads((root/'validation-report.json').read_text())
body+='<h2>Validation results and the cost of weaker assumptions</h2>'+table(['Profile','Evaluated weak labels','Selected','Same property','Different property'],[[v['profile'],v['evaluated'],v['selected'],v['same_property'],v['different_property']] for v in vr['profiles']])
body+='<p>An earlier audit caught seven false-uniqueness cases because the supplemental search missed Al Furjan records filed under Jabal Ali 1. The final search includes explicit community names in area, project and building fields, validated catalogue bridges, and ambiguous legal-area records as possible rivals. Final validation counts appear above. The corrected date-relaxed profile still has 12 different-property disagreements with earlier links: all involve the source saying Land while the reference DXBI transaction says Villa. This shows the risk of treating those types as decisive evidence. These history-based results remain review proposals. Earlier accepted links are still weak reference labels; zero disagreements does not prove real-world accuracy.</p>'
body+='<p><a href="Five-Group-Recovery-Experiment.xlsx">Open the full Excel workbook</a> · <a href="report-summary.json">Exact count data</a></p>'
css='body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;color:#20313f;background:#f5f7fa;margin:0 auto;padding:36px;max-width:1160px;line-height:1.55}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:42px}p{max-width:100ch}.lead{font-size:19px;color:#536473}.tiles{display:flex;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:28px 0}.tiles div{background:white;border:1px solid #dce3ea;border-radius:10px;padding:22px;flex:1;min-width:210px}.tiles strong{font-size:34px;display:block}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;background:white}th,td{padding:12px;text-align:left;border:1px solid #dce3ea}th{background:#234a62;color:white}details,article{background:white;border:1px solid #dce3ea;border-radius:8px;margin:12px 0;padding:18px}summary{font-weight:650;cursor:pointer}.compare{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}.compare section{background:#f5f7fa;padding:16px}dl{display:grid;grid-template-columns:135px 1fr;gap:7px}dt{color:#617180}dd{margin:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.good{border-left:6px solid #43875c}.conditional{border-left:6px solid #5977b5}.risk{border-left:6px solid #b16d63}h3,h4{margin-top:0}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:12px}@media(max-width:700px){body{padding:16px}.compare{grid-template-columns:1fr}table{font-size:11px}th,td{padding:6px}}'
(out/'Read-Me-Examples.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Five-group matching experiment</title><style>'+css+'</style><main>'+body+'</main></html>')
print(out/'Read-Me-Examples.html')
